Z||000000||MEL H. JOHNSON||11-17-2001||08:18 PM||||PLEASE GO TO E-BAY,SEARCH AUCTIONS BY NUMBER, PUNCH IN ITEM # 597520420 & TELL ME IF YOU WOULD EXPECT TO GET 2 HEAD LIGHT ASSEMBLIES TO BOLT IN & WORK WHEN PLUGGED IN?????     MEL||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-17-2001||08:23 PM||||From the description and the picture I would say that yes, a reasonable person would expect to bolt these into a car and have them work.<P>I'm assuming that this isn't the case.....are the motors shot or ??  Even if they need new drive pins you got them for a good price.  <P>Of course that isn't what's at issue here.  What's at issue is the descriptuion stated that they are in good working condition, so if they aren't then the item was misrepresented and you are entitled to get your money back.<P><BR>Good luck.<BR> <BR>Here's a link to the eBay page:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597520420%20&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597520420%20&r=0&t=0</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou||11-17-2001||08:29 PM||||Poorly described, I assume your mad cause you got no motors, as he listed them separetly. The ad should have said no motors and should not have said " in good working condition " as it may lead some to believe they had motors. <BR>"This auction is for a pair of headlight assemblies. These were removed from an '87 SE and are in good working condition. The lamps (bulbs) are Halogen. Buyer to pay $12.95 s/h (US 48) Payment with in 5 days of auction end via Paypal / Check / Money Order Happy Bidding and Good Luck!" <BR>Thats the way I see it, and I have 750 + feedbacks on eBay with no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMontreal||11-17-2001||08:35 PM||||They should be plug and play... motors in working order...<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-17-2001||08:50 PM||||Ahh.....I never would have suspected that the motors were not included!  <P>That is definitely a poorly written description.  It sounds like the seller was being vague on purpose.  If they were only the mechanisms and headlight bulbs then there was no real reason to state that it was from an '87 SE or that everything works.  He also should have made it known that the motors were not included.  This would have made it clear what was included and what wasn't.<P>Unfortunately with eBay there isn't much you can do except leave negative feedback (if the seller doesn't refund your $$).<P>Let us know if this gets resolved or not.    <BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou||11-17-2001||08:54 PM||||I don't think it was intentional I think thta he was listing so many items that he rushed the description without thinking it through. As often happens on ebay last minute bidders have very little time to research and bid before they ask questions. was this the case ? Still it is his fault for givng a poor description,  why should you be made to pay?||||reg||1
Z||000006||TRiAD||11-17-2001||09:44 PM||||I've seen a LOT of "shady" people on eBay.<P>You always have the right to EMAIL the seller with questions, prior to bidding...<P>This particular ad, WITH PIC, does not seem to be misleading. <P>Did you ecpect motors (that are not in the pic) to be included? And for that price?<P>I don't see it. Sorry. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||11-17-2001||09:57 PM||||Personally I think it is a semantic difference -- the definition of the word "assembly" or "assemblies" -- of the headlights work and the headlights themselves move up and down in the fashion they are intended to properly then technically the seller is correct. It can also be noted from the picture that there are no motors.<P>However, my feeling (and I have been a buyer/seller for over four years on eBay) is that the seller should have been more clear in his description. I don't think, however, that it was an intentional case of misrepresentation as the starting price was low and the reserve was low as well -- as we all know, a pair of headlight motors will go for more than $25.<P>When in doubt, email the seller and ask them the condition, what it includes or excludes or any other question you may have. Most sellers will be happy to respond to your questions as they are trying to sell the item.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||11-18-2001||06:53 AM||||Ive only had one problem selling on Ebay. I sold a ton of old diecast Nascars. Most were like 10-20 years old. One guy was wanting a refund because they were dusty inside and outside. I stated that they had been displayed on shelves since new and had no boxes. I told him to send it back for his refund, but he kept it anyway. FYI, someone bought a Dale Jarrett 'Citco' car for $175 that Id bought for $12. I about fell on the floor.||||reg||1
Z||000009||MEL H. JOHNSON||11-18-2001||05:36 PM||||THANKS A LOT GUYS!!! MY FEELING WAS IF THEY WORKED WELL WHEN REMOVED, THEY SHOULD WORK WHEN INSTALLED!!! I'M GOING THRU MEDIATION BECAUSE I REALLY FEEL THE ADD WAS MIS LEADING, BUT I'LL AGREE 100% WITH THE MEDIATOR!!! I DO AGREE YOU COULD GO BOTH WAYS, BUT IF I ADVERTISE A CAR AS RUNNING GOOD WHEN PARKED", I DON'T THINK YOU WOULD HAVE TO ASK IF IT HAD AN ENGINE, TRANS, & REAR END!!!    MEL||||reg||1
